sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch13-13> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Wherever a structure grows by permanent increments with unequal longitudinal growth about its axis, as in nails, claws, beaks and teeth, it always tends to the form of a logarithmic spiral, which becomes conspicuous only when the structure is long.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Claws, beaks and teeth grown by unequal permanent accretion are logarithmic spirals";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "unequal longitudinal growth by permanent increments \\Rightarrow r = a e^{\\theta\\cot\\alpha}";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XIII, “The Shapes of Horns, and of Teeth or Tusks: with a Note on Torsion”; topic “Teeth, beak and claw”. Scope: nails, claws, beaks, incisors, canines and tusks of vertebrates"
}
